 hypersurface Calabi-Yau fourfold $Y_4.$ We show that it is possible to find a toric hypersurface Calabi-Yau in which there are more than $h^{1,1}(Y_4)$ non-perturbative superpotential terms with trivial intermediate Jacobian. Hodge numbers of divisors in toric CICYs are the subjects of the part two.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"control_number":1889496,"dois":[{"source":"Springer","value":"10.1007/JHEP03(2022)168"},{"material":"publication","source":"arXiv","value":"10.1007/JHEP03(2022)168"}],"preprint_date":"2021-07-20","arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["hep-th","math.AG"],"value":"2107.09779"}],"titles":[{"source":"Springer","title":"A note on h$^{2,1}$ of divisors in CY fourfolds. Part I"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"A Note on $h^{2,1}$ of Divisors of CY Fourfolds I"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"A Note on $h^{2,1}$ of divisors of CY Fourfolds I"}],"document_type":["article"]},"id":"1889496","links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1889496?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1889496?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1889496?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1889496?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1889496?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1889496?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A1889496"},"updated":"2024-09-27T18:04:33.221785+00:00"}],"total":1},"links":{"self":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3A2107.09779&size=5&page=1&fields=titles,authors,dois,publication_info,arxiv_eprints,document_type,preprint_date,imprints,abstracts,urls","bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3A2107.09779&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3A2107.09779&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3A2107.09779&size=5&page=1&fo